(their equation (8.2)) that is established \emph{inside the proof} of their Lemma~8.5 \cite[\S8]{lv2018}. The published
\emph{statement} of that lemma bounds only the smaller max-residue sum. That proof in turn relies on Harper's Facts 8.8--8.12 (a
preprint, \cite{harper2012}) and on a treatment of Siegel/Page characters, which we use at $u\asymp(\log N/\log\log N)^{1/2}$. Two independent
analytic referees checked this import against the sources and found it valid in our regime: the ranges hold with fixed power margins, and
$u/\log^2u\gg\log\log x$, so the logarithmic losses are absorbed. Both nevertheless named it the weakest link of the whole argument. A self-contained proof of Part~1,
